s for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4184\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the offer department name, the number of distinct subjects offered by the department in the academic year 2012, and for each subject that was offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", display the subject key, subject title, academic year, term description, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, and the deviation of each subject's enrollment number from the average enrollment number for its subject key group, ordered by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3644\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a total of 1 unit, show the subject title from the summary, the course number from the offered table, the subject title from the offered summary, the department name from the summary, the offer department name from the offered summary, the row number within each department name group ordered by subject title from the summary, and for each department, also provide the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student). List the results ordered by department name and row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2958\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, among subjects that are not repeatable, what is the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by each department? List the academic year, department name, average enrollment, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), ordered by variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4683\", \"desc\": \"For each department where the total number of subject enrollments for subjects offered in the current term is greater than 10, and for each course number in that department where the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2, provide the department name, the total number of subject enrollments, the course number, the number of unique library subjects offered, the minimum total units for those subjects, and the name of the responsible faculty member for each course. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1335\", \"desc\": \"List, for each department, either (a) the department's full name, the range and variance of the total units for degree-granting Mathematics department courses offered in the 2008 academic year along with the long course description for each course (with the reason 'Math 2008 Stats'), or (b) the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units) where the average total units is greater than the overall average across all departments (with the reason 'High Avg Units'). Show the columns in the following order: department name, total units range, total units variance, average total units, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, long course description, and reason for inclusion. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4812\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 combinations of department name, subject code, and course number (where the department is degree granting and the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2) with the highest number of unique library subjects offered, display the department name, subject code, number of subject codes, minimum department budget code, course number, number of unique library subjects offered, minimum total units, the subject title with the most enrolled students for that course, and the corresponding number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4527\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with a non-null subject code description), and, for each subject in 2021 offered by these departments in the School of Engineering, list the subject id, subject title, and the number of enrolled students, but only include subjects where the number of enrolled students exceeds the average enrollment for that department in 2021. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3632\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", show the subject title, subject key, offer department name, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, subject ID, academic year, term description, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row, ordered by offer department name and academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3356\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subject titles by the number of reserved library materials for subjects offered in the term '2009SP', what are the subject title, the offering department name, the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with a non-null subject code description), and the count of reserved materials? Please provide the subject title, the offering department name, the variance, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), and the count of reserved materials, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3493\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook, show the subject code, subject number, department name, subject title, term description, total units, the average subject enrollment number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by department code and ordered by total units, the textbook material key, the textbook material status key, and the row number of the course within each department ordered by subject code. List the results in order by department name, subject code, and subject number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2597\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the description of the academic year, the department name, the average total units for all subjects offered by that department in terms that match that academic year and have a term status indicator of 'P', and the deviation of each department's average total units from the overall average total units for that academic year? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4724\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the library in the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Additionally, for the corresponding offering department and school, provide the number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ' and the minimum total units for those subjects. Also, include the department phone number and the school name for the offering department, and display the responsible faculty name for each subject. The columns should be shown in the following order: subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, maximum total units for each row and the next two rows, number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ', minimum total units for those subjects, department phone number, school name, and responsible faculty name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2461\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 subjects offered by the Chemistry department (Course 5) with the highest number of enrolled students, display each subject's title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, term code, material status key, the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject ID, and the department most represented among the responsible faculty for these subjects along with the count of subjects from that department. For each such subject, also provide the corresponding academic term parameter, the term description, the average total units, and the variance of total units of all subjects offered in the corresponding effective term, considering only subjects that are offered this year and are in the Mathematics department. The columns should be: subject title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, term code, material status key, maximum number of enrolled students, most prominent responsible faculty department, count of subjects from that department, academic term parameter, term description, average total units, and variance of total units. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2272\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the average of the total units, the range of the total units, the variance of the total units for courses with total units greater than 0, and for each course level, what is the number of unique students and the minimum CIP program code among their courses, considering only degree-granting departments? Additionally, for each course level, what is the average number of lecture units and the maximum number of lab units for Mathematics courses? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4305\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subjects offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\" that have the highest number of enrolled students, display each subject's offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, the number of enrolled students, and the rank of each subject within its offering department (ordered by subject offered key), but only include subjects where the offering department is among those that, in the term with code '2022SU', had an average total units for their subjects greater than the average total units for all subjects offered in that term. List the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, term description, number of enrolled students, and the rank within the department, in that order, and order the results by department name and number of enrolled students descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4602\", \"desc\": \"Show the department full names, subject titles, total units, and the number of unique course materials per subject for subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering. For each subject, also provide the material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, course number description, offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each row considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by material key, where the subject title and department code match between the subject and course material datasets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1023\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year where the Mathematics department has at least one unique subject with subject enrollment number greater than 10, what are the academic year, academic year description, department name, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, variance of total units, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units for subjects offered in the fall term that are not variable units and are offered by the Mathematics department? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4640\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term '2017JA', what is the subject title, the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the offering department name, the department full name, the school name, the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department code, the coefficient of variation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with at least one enrolled student), and the department's school code? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4387\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the School of Engineering with total student enrollment in its courses greater than the average total enrollment across all Engineering departments (and with total enrollment greater than 50), display the department name, the total number of students enrolled in its courses, and the highest average total units for subjects it has ever offered in a regular academic term, listing the results in descending order of total enrollment. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3868\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the School of Engineering where the total number of students enrolled in courses offered by that department is greater than the average total enrollment across all Engineering departments (and the total enrollment is greater than 50), show the department name and total enrollment, and for each such department, show the library reserve material details with material status key equal to 'U', including the library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, the tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, the subject title, the minimum tip material status key in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the number of enrolled students, as well as the responsible faculty name and the offer department name, for materials offered by that department. The columns should be: department name, total enrollment, library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, subject title, windowed minimum tip material status key, responsible faculty name, and offer department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2335\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level, where the total number of enrolled students in offered subjects is greater than 10, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of unique courses, the minimum total units among those subjects that are degree-granting courses, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for Mathematics courses (considering only departments that offer more than five courses), and the number of unique subject codes for Mathematics in the SIS_SUBJECT_CODE table. List the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, and the number of unique subject codes, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2158\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the 2022 academic year by a degree-granting department, specifically in the Department of Mathematics (Course 18) and excluding subjects offered by the Department of Physics, provide the subject ID, subject title, department name, the number of enrolled students, the total number of lecture units, and, for each subject, indicate whether it is also offered as a joint subject with another department. Additionally, show the range and variance of the total units for letter graded subjects offered this year in the Mathematics department. List the results in order of subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3668\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering, show the subject title, total units, department full name, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title. Additionally, for each matching course material detail, provide the material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, the course number description, the offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each row considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by material key. The results should include the subject title, total units, department full name, window row number, material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, course number description, offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students, in that order, for subjects and course materials where the subject title and department code match between the two datasets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3530\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term with code '2012SU', show the subject title, subject ID, offer department name, academic year, term description, the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the academic year, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for that subject (considering only subjects offered by the \\\"Harvard Cross-Enrollment Prog\\\" department and with more than 5 offerings). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3867\", \"desc\": \"For each subject in a department where the school code and subject title are not null, and for each subject offered in the 2022FA term with total units greater than the average for that term, display the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, the number of subjects in the same department, the subject ID, the term description, and the running sum of total units for that academic year, ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3664\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subject titles by the number of reserved library materials for subjects offered in the term '2009SP', display each subject title, the offering department name, the count of reserved materials, the academic year, the department name, the average of the total units, and the variance of the total units for subjects offered in regular terms, with the columns shown in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}}"
