erials offered by that department. The columns should be: department name, total enrollment, library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, subject title, windowed minimum tip material status key, responsible faculty name, and offer department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3078\", \"desc\": \"For each subject title and department name where the total units are greater than 3, give the number of offered sections, the minimum number of enrolled students, and the average lab units for those subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3901\", \"desc\": \"For each offer department code in the 2012SU term with total units greater than 0, list the subject title, course number, department name, the dense rank over the offer department code, the course, course description, school name, program code, program title, category code, category title, four digit code, four digit title, and the minimum warehouse load date from the CIP table over each category code group for courses in department 6, and include a grand total of subjects per offer department code and a grand total for all courses in each school in the format (nulls for subject-specific fields, department name, total subjects, course-specific fields, school name, and total courses). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3493\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook, show the subject code, subject number, department name, subject title, term description, total units, the average subject enrollment number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by department code and ordered by total units, the textbook material key, the textbook material status key, and the row number of the course within each department ordered by subject code. List the results in order by department name, subject code, and subject number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2591\", \"desc\": \"For all subjects in the 2014FA term with at least one enrolled student, show the subject title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, the TIP material status key, the total number of units, and the minimum total number of units in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the course number, along with the cluster type description and the HGN code description for each subject. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3398\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the same term as a TIP detail record with material status 'RQ', show the subject key, subject title, offer department name, TIP material key, and the rank of each record within each offer department name group ordered by subject key, along with the subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject key, where the subject, term, and offer department name match in both cases. List the columns in the following order: subject key, subject title, offer department name, TIP material key, rank, subject title (from the second subquery), subject ID, offer department name (from the second subquery), offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3393\", \"desc\": \"For subjects with at least 5 enrolled students that are offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, number of enrolled students, term code, material status key, ISBN, row number within each material status group ordered by subject ID, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, ordered by offering department name, material status key, and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3911\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, total number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, as well as the maximum windowed average record count from tip detail records with material status key 'RQ' (using a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by financial aid year). Additionally, for each offering department, include a grand total row showing the total number of enrolled students across all its subjects (with nulls for subject ID and subject title), and the corresponding maximum windowed average record count if available. Order the results by offering department name and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3236\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering that are also offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, total units, department full name, the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, department full name for the term, subject code, subject code description, and the minimum number of enrolled students over each subject code group, ordered by subject title and subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3904\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code where the department is degree granting, show the subject code, subject code description, department name (from subject code), school name, the number of subject codes per school name and whether the subject code description is present ('Has Description') or missing ('No Description'), and for each matching department in subjects offered in the term with code '2022SU', show the subject's ID, total units, department name (from subject offered), and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. For each school name, include a grand total for all subject codes in the format of (null, null, null, school name, null, total subject codes, null, null, null, null). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4405\", \"desc\": \"For each combination of activity and department/academic year enrollment statistics, list the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, category description, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the category name and ordered by the category name, along with the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects offered (subject count), minimum number of total units for those subjects, and the average number of enrolled students per subject (for departments and academic years where the number of enrolled students in a subject is greater than 5). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4911\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering with the highest maximum enrolled students (considering the current and next 2 rows ordered by subject key), display each subject's title, total units, department full name, row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the department that offered the subject. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4756\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and for each department, the number of subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3273\", \"desc\": \"For courses in the School of Engineering with a total of 12 units, display the course number, course description, subject title, total units, offering department name, the row number of the course within its offering department ordered by course number, and the dense rank of the subject (considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by total units) if available. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1393\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3248\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units that are also offered in the library by the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each subject within its department ordered by subject code, the number of enrolled students, offering department name, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\