record counter variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1393\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4826\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material with material status key 'U', list the subject ID, library course instructor key, term description, academic year, term start date, the minimum academic year in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by library reserve catalog key, the library subject offered key, the tip material key, the tip material status key, the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the tip material status key and ordered by the academic year, and for each, include the academic year description and the last day of final exam from the ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL table, and calculate the normalized year to average record count ratio (academic year divided by average record count in the window), ordered by the normalized year to average record count ratio descending.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3357\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material detail with material status key 'U', show the reserve catalog key, subject offered key, term code, academic year, term description, tip material key, tip material status key, and the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the tip material status key and ordered by the academic year, along with the corresponding textbook material in the TIP_DETAIL table with material status key 'RQ' that matches on tip material key and academic year, showing the textbook subject offered key, textbook material key, subject ID, textbook academic year, textbook term description, and the row number within each textbook academic year group ordered by term code. Present the results in the order of reserve material academic year descending and textbook row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4701\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the academic year, academic year description, the geometric mean of the number of library reserve material details per subject offered (considering only records where the material status is 'U' and the academic term is a regular term), the average total units, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, and the average number of design units for subjects that are offered in the fall term and have a material status of 'U' in the library reserve? List the results ordered by the geometric mean of materials per subject in descending order, then by the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3868\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the School of Engineering where the total number of students enrolled in courses offered by that department is greater than the average total enrollment across all Engineering departments (and the total enrollment is greater than 50), show the department name and total enrollment, and for each such department, show the library reserve material details with material status key equal to 'U', including the library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, the tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, the subject title, the minimum tip material status key in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the number of enrolled students, as well as the responsible faculty name and the offer department name, for materials offered by that department. The columns should be: department name, total enrollment, library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, subject title, windowed minimum tip material status key, responsible faculty name, and offer department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3356\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subject titles by the number of reserved library materials for subjects offered in the term '2009SP', what are the subject title, the offering department name, the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with a non-null subject code description), and the count of reserved materials? Please provide the subject title, the offering department name, the variance, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), and the count of reserved materials, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2597\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the description of the academic year, the department name, the average total units for all subjects offered by that department in terms that match that academic year and have a term status indicator of 'P', and the deviation of each department's average total units from the overall average total units for that academic year? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4724\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the library in the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Additionally, for the corresponding offering department and school, provide the number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ' and the minimum total units for those subjects. Also, include the department phone number and the school name for the offering department, and display the responsible faculty name for each subject. The columns should be shown in the following order: subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, maximum total units for each row and the next two rows, number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ', minimum total units for those subjects, department phone number, school name, and responsible faculty name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4978\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material detail with material status key 'U', show the reserve catalog key, subject offered key, term code, academic year, term description, tip material key, tip material status key, and the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the tip material status key and ordered by the academic year, along with the corresponding textbook material in the TIP_DETAIL table with material status key 'RQ' that matches on tip material key and academic year, showing the textbook subject offered key, textbook material key, subject ID, textbook academic year, textbook term description, and the row number within each textbook academic year group ordered by term code. Additionally, for each matching textbook material, include the term start date and term end date from the ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL table. Present the results in the order of reserve material academic year descending and textbook row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3664\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subject titles by the number of reserved library materials for subjects offered in the term '2009SP', display each subject title, the offering department name, the count of reserved materials, the academic year, the department name, the average of the total units, and the variance of the total units for subjects offered in regular terms, with the columns shown in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2958\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, among subjects that are not repeatable, what is the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by each department? List the academic year, department name, average enrollment, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), ordered by variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4287\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material detail with material status key equal to 'U' and for subjects offered in the term with code '2025FA', show the library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, the tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, the subject title from the subject offered table, the minimum tip material status key in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the number of enrolled students (only including those where the number of enrolled students is greater than the average across all subjects), the offering department name, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, the offering school name, and the responsible faculty name for each subject. Order the results by offering department and descending number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1335\", \"desc\": \"List, for each department, either (a) the department's full name, the range and variance of the total units for degree-granting Mathematics department courses offered in the 2008 academic year along with the long course description for each course (with the reason 'Math 2008 Stats'), or (b) the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units) where the average total units is greater than the overall average across all departments (with the reason 'High Avg Units'). Show the columns in the following order: department name, total units range, total units variance, average total units, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, long course description, and reason for inclusion. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2272\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the average of the total units, the range of the total units, the variance of the total units for courses with total units greater than 0, and for each course level, what is the number of unique students and the minimum CIP program code among their courses, considering only degree-granting departments? Additionally, for each course level, what is the average number of lecture units and the maximum number of lab units for Mathematics courses? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2895\", \"desc\": \"For each subject that has a library material status of 'U' and a tip material status of 'RQ', what is the minimum library material status key, the total record count, and the most recent warehouse load date from both the library reserve and tip detail tables? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4683\", \"desc\": \"For each department where the total number of subject enrollments for subjects offered in the current term is greater than 10, and for each course number in that department where the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2, provide the department name, the total number of subject enrollments, the course number, the number of unique library subjects offered, the minimum total units for those subjects, and the name of the responsible faculty member for each course. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2151\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees (excluding the Biology department), provide the department name, the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, and, if the department is Political Science, also include for each HGN code the maximum number of lecture units among all subjects in the course catalog and the subject title from the subject offered table for subjects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_41\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, provide the academic year description and calculate the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered in terms that are not the current term, have a term status indicator of 'P', are offered by the Mathematics department, and are full term subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2180\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2014FA' by the Chemistry department, show the subject title from the library, the number of enrolled students in the library subject, the responsible faculty name from the TIP subject, the offer department name from the TIP subject, the minimum number of enrolled students in the library subject within a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the TIP subject's responsible faculty MIT ID, and for each academic year, also show the academic year and academic year description and the coefficient of variation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects in the Mathematics department (Course 18) that have more than 0 total units and are offered in terms with a term status indicator of 'P'. Additionally, for each Chemistry subject, include the number of required TIP materials (where TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'RQ') for that subject in that term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4061\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, show the department name, academic year, academic year description, and the geometric mean of the total units for all subjects offered by the department in regular terms with total units greater than zero, along with, for each academic building where these subjects are held and which has rooms larger than 40 square meters, the building name, the average, range, and variance of the room areas, as well as the total assignable area of the building and the year the building was built. The results are ordered by department name, academic year (descending), and room area range (descending). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3493\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook, show the subject code, subject number, department name, subject title, term description, total units, the average subject enrollment number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by department code and ordered by total units, the textbook material key, the textbook material status key, and the row number of the course within each department ordered by subject code. List the results in order by department name, subject code, and subject number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1301\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, where the maximum number of total units for any Mathematics (Course 18) subject offered in that year is greater than 9 and there are more than 5 Mathematics subjects offered in the fall term, what are the academic year, the maximum total units, the corresponding term description, the subject title, the academic year description, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in library subjects offered during terms in that year, and the average number of equivalent subjects for those library subjects? List the results in order of academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1288\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the maximum enrollment for IAP activities offered in that year by the Mathematics department, considering only activities that require advance sign-up and are not cancelled, and also provide the academic year description? For each department, include a grand total for all activities in the format of (department name, null, total variance and stddev). Additionally, for each such department, provide the department code, the department name, and the total number of enrolled students in both the library and tip subject offerings, but only for those departments where the total number of enrolled students is more than one standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) above the mean total enrolled students across all departments, and restrict your answer to departments whose name is 'Mathematics' (Course 18). Also, for each such department, list the names of the responsible faculty members from both the library and tip subject offerings. The columns to display, in order, are: department name, academic year description, total variance, total standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, department name, total enrolled, library faculty, and tip faculty. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4602\", \"desc\": \"Show the department full names, subject titles, total units, and the number of unique course materials per subject for subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering. For each subject, also provide the material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, course number description, offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each row considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by material key, where the subject title and department code match between the subject and course material datasets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4448\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the department name, the highest total units among its subjects with exactly 12 units in the Fall Term 2024-2025, and for each course in that department that was offered in 2022 and has at least one required or optional textbook and has total units greater than the average for such courses, show the course's subject code, subject number, subject title, the term description, the textbook material key, the textbook material status key, and the row number within the department ordered by subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3644\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a total of 1 unit, show the subject title from the summary, the course number from the offered table, the subject title from the offered summary, the department name from the summary, the offer department name from the offered summary, the row number within each department name group ordered by subject title from the summary, and for each department, also provide the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student). List the results ordered by department name and row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1471\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units in the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject code, subject title, department name, school name, and the rank within each school name group ordered by subject code, but only include those subjects whose total units exceed the average total units for their respective school. Additionally, for the Mathematics department, also show the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects that are offered this year, are letter graded, and are in the Mathematics department), as well as the number of subjects that are Communication Intensive (i.e., have a non-null COMM_REQ_ATTRIBUTE), with these statistics included for each subject in the result. Present the columns in the following order: subject code, subject title, department name, school name, rank within school, average total units, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), and number of Communication Intensive subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}}"
